250
00:11:45,567 --> 00:11:46,833
- [Pearl] I'm actually just

251
00:11:46,833 --> 00:11:48,267
apartment-sitting
for my brother.

252
00:11:49,733 --> 00:11:52,200
- [Tom] Welcome. I like to
call it the plague nest.

253
00:11:54,633 --> 00:11:55,933
- Wie heisst du?

254
00:11:55,933 --> 00:12:00,100
(Crow makes random
babbling noises)

255
00:12:00,100 --> 00:12:02,033
- [Pearl] He's the
lost member of ZZ Top.

256
00:12:05,067 --> 00:12:07,000
- So, you have no name.

257
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:08,400
- [Tom] if I lit
your head on fire,

258
00:12:08,400 --> 00:12:09,733
would that jog your memory?

259
00:12:13,433 --> 00:12:14,433
- Time for food.

260
00:12:14,433 --> 00:12:15,833
- [Crow] Hope you like rats.

261
00:12:17,233 --> 00:12:18,133
- English, eh?

262
00:12:20,167 --> 00:12:21,633
my name is Baydool.

263
00:12:21,633 --> 00:12:24,567
- [Tom] Oh no, wait, that's
my intestinal condition.

264
00:12:24,567 --> 00:12:26,567
- Can you say Baydool?

265
00:12:26,567 --> 00:12:27,600
- [Pearl] Let me try.

266
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:29,900
Get bent. No, I guess I can't.

267
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:38,167
- You're no longer
a slave, understand?

268
00:12:38,167 --> 00:12:40,167
- [Crow] You're the
hostage of a madman.

269
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:45,300
- This is your home now.

270
00:12:45,300 --> 00:12:46,900
- [Pearl] You'll
live in this basket.

271
00:12:46,900 --> 00:12:48,633
- You have a roof
over your head.

272
00:12:48,633 --> 00:12:50,800
Keeps out the rain,
most of the time anyway.

273
00:12:52,433 --> 00:12:53,900
There's always
food on the table.

274
00:12:53,900 --> 00:12:55,767
- [Crow] And food in my beard.

275
00:12:55,767 --> 00:12:57,300
- Would you like some food?

276
00:12:57,300 --> 00:12:59,200
- [Tom] I would but what's
that crap you're holding up?

277
00:13:02,033 --> 00:13:03,300
- All you have to do is ask.

278
00:13:03,300 --> 00:13:05,267
- [Pearl] And so help
me, I'll put you down.

279
00:13:10,333 --> 00:13:12,267
- [Tom] Ah, it's Martin Landau.

280
00:13:12,267 --> 00:13:13,467
- it's a disguise.

281
00:13:15,933 --> 00:13:18,067
There are times when
you need a disguise.

282
00:13:18,067 --> 00:13:19,867
Disguises come in
handy now and then.

283
00:13:19,867 --> 00:13:21,967
- [Crow] like when you're
cruising Sunset Boulevard.

284
00:13:21,967 --> 00:13:23,367
- [Baydool] Don't be afraid.

285
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:27,800
- [Pearl] I'll see if
Bombadil has a place to crash.

286
00:13:30,467 --> 00:13:32,800
- [Tom] No, it's
Joe Walsh! Aaah!

287
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:36,467
(instrumental theme music)

288
00:13:39,233 --> 00:13:41,433
- [Crow] Robert Bork
takes a constitutional.

289
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:46,900
- [Pearl] He's a living
Dr. Seuss character.

290
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:50,400
- [Tom] Oh please, no, no!

291
00:13:54,767 --> 00:13:56,633
- [Crow] What's he
pulling out!? Help!

292
00:14:01,567 --> 00:14:03,500
- [Pearl] Eww, wizard whiz.

293
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:05,033
- [Crow] He drained the wizard.

294
00:14:13,967 --> 00:14:15,900
(disgusted exclamations)

295
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:17,700
- I beg your pardon, sir.

296
00:14:17,700 --> 00:14:19,600
(indistinct)

297
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:21,233
Come inside boy, there's
all sorts of rubbish

298
00:14:21,233 --> 00:14:22,967
in the streets at this hour.

299
00:14:22,967 --> 00:14:24,467
- [Tom] That's my pee!

300
00:14:24,467 --> 00:14:27,100
- [Crow] The pee throwing
scene. ladies and gentlemen.

301
00:14:31,867 --> 00:14:33,133
- [Pearl] Now I'm
going to attach

302
00:14:33,133 --> 00:14:34,700
Rosey Grier's head
to your shoulder.

303
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:36,833
- [Tom] You're funny.

304
00:14:36,833 --> 00:14:38,767
I like you.
- You bet I am.

305
00:14:39,900 --> 00:14:42,200
- [Crow] You gave us a mint.
- Yeah.

306
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:43,000
- Excuse me?

307
00:14:45,133 --> 00:14:46,367
- My name is Travis.

308
00:14:46,367 --> 00:14:48,667
- [Crow] Man, do
you ever shut up?

309
00:14:48,667 --> 00:14:50,867
- Travis.
(cracking)

310
00:14:51,833 --> 00:14:52,833
- [Pearl] Oh, sorry.

311
00:14:54,433 --> 00:14:55,267
- That's a fine name.

312
00:14:55,267 --> 00:14:56,267
- [Tom] If you're gay.

313
00:14:58,867 --> 00:15:01,100
- How is it you came
to be sold as a slave?

314
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:02,633
- [Crow] I accidentally
put a sign on myself

315
00:15:02,633 --> 00:15:04,467
that read "slave for sale."

316
00:15:07,633 --> 00:15:08,933
- A big battle was coming.

317
00:15:11,667 --> 00:15:13,667
My father sent us to safety.

318
00:15:13,667 --> 00:15:15,600
- [Pearl] He wasn't
very good at that.

319
00:15:15,600 --> 00:15:16,633
- They attacked.

320
00:15:18,900 --> 00:15:20,600
- It's all right now, Travis.

321
00:15:22,233 --> 00:15:23,900
All is well.

322
00:15:23,900 --> 00:15:25,967
- [Tom] Oh yeah I got bought
by a beard-wearing psycho,

323
00:15:25,967 --> 00:15:27,367
had half a can of
pee thrown at me,

324
00:15:27,367 --> 00:15:28,533
yeah, things are great.

325
00:15:31,233 --> 00:15:32,067
- Call me Tee.

326
00:15:33,633 --> 00:15:35,267
- [Crow] Huh,
kid's kind of dumb.

327
00:15:39,900 --> 00:15:40,833
- [Pearl] And during the day

328
00:15:40,833 --> 00:15:42,600
I'm a Stevie Nicks impersonator.

329
00:15:45,300 --> 00:15:47,200
- [Tom] No, Gaul is
that way, damn it.

330
00:15:48,900 --> 00:15:51,467
- [Crow] Pots, pots for
throwing pee at your neighbors.

331
00:15:57,400 --> 00:15:59,333
- [Pearl] Good news,
only 20% of the village

332
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:01,467
died of the plague overnight.

333
00:16:05,200 --> 00:16:07,167
- [Tom] Can someone
spare some coffee?

334
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:12,700
- [Crow] A latte, anyone?
I'll even take decaf.

335
00:16:14,700 --> 00:16:16,867
- [Pearl] Here you are,
toenail clipping then.

336
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:21,333
- [Tom] Back now, this
is a lot of money.

337
00:16:24,067 --> 00:16:25,467
- [Crow] Hey, a wheat penny.

338
00:16:29,233 --> 00:16:31,467
- [Pearl] I got some
lint and a bloody molar.

339
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,133
- [Tom] Hurry up, I gotta

340
00:16:34,133 --> 00:16:35,733
fly a Sopwith Camel in a minute.

341
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:41,100
- [Crow] Halt, Sir
Dan of Blocker.

342
00:16:44,833 --> 00:16:48,167
♪ Master Bojangles, beg ♪

343
00:16:49,667 --> 00:16:52,000
- [Tom] That's great, Pearl.

344
00:16:56,233 --> 00:16:58,500
Ah, my pyramid begging
scheme is working.

345
00:17:00,800 --> 00:17:02,867
- [Crow] Watch, I'm gonna
kill all the ants, watch.

346
00:17:06,600 --> 00:17:08,500
- [Tom] Bring in da
noise, bring in da funk.

347
00:17:08,500 --> 00:17:09,667
- [Pearl] I think the funk

348
00:17:09,667 --> 00:17:11,367
is pretty well covered
by these folks.

349
00:17:17,267 --> 00:17:19,133
- [Crow] We make
less when you dance.

350
00:17:28,200 --> 00:17:30,100
- [Tom] I could buy
and sell your ass.

351
00:17:34,267 --> 00:17:36,667
- [Pearl] Oh, the
medieval Deney Terrio.

352
00:17:39,300 --> 00:17:40,967
- [Crow] Cat heads for the rats.

353
00:17:40,967 --> 00:17:42,533
- Food!

354
00:17:42,533 --> 00:17:43,767
I'll be right back.

355
00:17:48,167 --> 00:17:50,267
- [Tom] We heard about
the kid who dances.

356
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:53,267
We're from the
William Morris Agency.

357
00:17:56,100 --> 00:18:01,100
(villagers yelling)_

358
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:03,700
- [Pearl] Alan Hale!

359
00:18:03,700 --> 00:18:05,233
- [Man] At your
service, Lord Vultare.

360
00:18:05,233 --> 00:18:07,600
- [Vultare] Shut up and get
these criminals to the brig.

361
00:18:08,933 --> 00:18:11,567
Now, let the fate
of these wretches

362
00:18:11,567 --> 00:18:13,567
serve as a lesson to you all!

363
00:18:13,567 --> 00:18:15,700
Insurrection will
not be tolerated

364
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:18,267
in the land of the Mannerjay.

365
00:18:18,267 --> 00:18:19,200
- Murderer!

366
00:18:20,533 --> 00:18:22,700
- [Tom] Aw, they killed
her personal Smurf.

367
00:18:24,100 --> 00:18:25,733
- Murderer!

368
00:18:25,733 --> 00:18:28,233
- [Pearl] He was
a great peasant!

369
00:18:28,233 --> 00:18:30,133
- What is that?

370
00:18:30,133 --> 00:18:30,967
- Lord Vultare.

371
00:18:32,733 --> 00:18:34,733
- [Tom] last week on "Knights."

372
00:18:36,433 --> 00:18:37,667
- He's the one.

373
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:40,167
- The one, Tee?

374
00:18:41,233 --> 00:18:42,067
- [Crow] Safe!

375
00:18:46,233 --> 00:18:50,067
♪ Oooooklahoma where the wind ♪

376
00:18:51,167 --> 00:18:52,367
- He killed my mother.

377
00:18:52,367 --> 00:18:53,800
- [Vultare] Oh,
stop that. Stop it.

378
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:55,367
Guard, have these
people dispersed

379
00:18:55,367 --> 00:18:57,000
or I'll arrest them as spies!

380
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:05,067
- [Pearl] He's
reading "Ye Firm,"

381
00:19:05,067 --> 00:19:06,000
- Who's Cato?

382
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:07,867
- [Crow] Clouseau's house boy.

383
00:19:07,867 --> 00:19:10,333
- You can read. Tee,
that's magnificent.

384
00:19:11,267 --> 00:19:12,200
Where did you learn?

385
00:19:12,200 --> 00:19:14,033
- [Tom] Hooked on Phonics.

386
00:19:14,033 --> 00:19:15,467
- Don't be afraid, you can read.

387
00:19:15,467 --> 00:19:16,667
it's wonderful.

388
00:19:16,667 --> 00:19:18,367
- [Pearl] Read me
"Portnoy's Complaint."

389
00:19:18,367 --> 00:19:19,800
- Who taught you?

390
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:21,833
- No one.

391
00:19:23,233 --> 00:19:24,600
- You taught yourself?

392
00:19:24,600 --> 00:19:27,400
- [Crow] Well, I can
only read the word Cato.

393
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:32,400
- From lands far to the
north will come a young sage.

394
00:19:33,833 --> 00:19:35,400
- [Tom] Oh, Garrison Keillor.

395
00:19:35,400 --> 00:19:36,200
- Pardon me?

396
00:19:39,833 --> 00:19:43,833
- This is an atlas,
there are maps in it.

397
00:19:43,833 --> 00:19:46,467
- [Pearl] Uh yeah, that
would be an atlas, yes.

398
00:19:46,467 --> 00:19:47,433
- England.

399
00:19:47,433 --> 00:19:48,400
- [Crow] Dan & John Ford Coley.

400
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:50,433
- You can read maps as well?

401
00:19:50,433 --> 00:19:53,233
- Our manor house was
just outside London.

402
00:19:53,233 --> 00:19:54,733
- Your manor house, really?

403
00:19:54,733 --> 00:19:56,667
- [Tom] He's trying to
get himself invited.

404
00:19:58,033 --> 00:20:01,000
- No, not master, Tee.

405
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:03,600
You're free now, you're no
longer a slave, remember.

406
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:07,933
- My mother taught me
those whom we respect,

407
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:12,867
those with great wisdom and
dignity, we should call master.

408
00:20:12,867 --> 00:20:14,100
- [Crow] Right Mr. Bater?

409
00:20:15,167 --> 00:20:16,367
- I can live with that.

410
00:20:16,367 --> 00:20:18,233
- [Tom] I can also
live with my scabies.

411
00:20:21,067 --> 00:20:23,100
- [Pearl] Aah, another
plague-ridden day.

412
00:20:24,833 --> 00:20:26,133
- [Crow] Rubber Soul font.

413
00:20:30,333 --> 00:20:31,167
What the?

414
00:20:33,100 --> 00:20:34,600
Please hammer, don't hurt him.

415
00:20:37,133 --> 00:20:39,733
- Go on, go on. You
know what I want.

416
00:20:39,733 --> 00:20:41,800
Fix it and bring it
back before nightfall.

417
00:20:43,833 --> 00:20:44,800
- [Pearl] Hey how's
it going Pete?

418
00:20:44,800 --> 00:20:46,367
- [Crow] Not bad, Charlie.

419
00:20:46,367 --> 00:20:47,733
- Well, what is it?

420
00:20:48,933 --> 00:20:51,000
Don't stand there
flapping your jaws.

421
00:20:52,467 --> 00:20:54,600
Have I responded to
the Emperor of Cathay?

422
00:20:54,600 --> 00:20:56,100
- Yes, your ladyship,

423
00:20:56,100 --> 00:20:57,933
- What did I say?

424
00:20:57,933 --> 00:21:01,667
- You refused him,
your ladyship, again.

425
00:21:01,667 --> 00:21:04,367
- Of course I did, he's
dull and diminutive.

426
00:21:04,367 --> 00:21:05,933
- [Tom] Danny DeVito?

427
00:21:05,933 --> 00:21:06,933
- What else?

428
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:13,500
- As your ladyship ordered,
Lord Vultare is waiting.

429
00:21:14,367 --> 00:21:16,133
- How long has he been waiting?

430
00:21:16,133 --> 00:21:18,267
- Since midday, your ladyship.

431
00:21:19,733 --> 00:21:21,400
- [Pearl] She's a Merv
Griffin production.

432
00:21:21,400 --> 00:21:23,967
- It will have to do, I suppose.

433
00:21:23,967 --> 00:21:25,200
Send him in.

434
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:28,933
♪ A time for us to
be in a crappy film ♪

435
00:21:28,933 --> 00:21:31,600
- Doesn't she know who
she's meddling with?

436
00:21:31,600 --> 00:21:33,300
- [Man] Well, evidently
not, your grace.

437
00:21:33,300 --> 00:21:34,800
- The Panther of the Pyrenees.

438
00:21:36,567 --> 00:21:37,800
The Scourge of Iberia.

439
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:39,267
- [Crow] The Sultan of Swing.

440
00:21:41,767 --> 00:21:43,967
- I am forever your humble
servant, your loveliness.

441
00:21:43,967 --> 00:21:45,300
- [Crow] Hi.

442
00:21:45,300 --> 00:21:47,467
- Her ladyship will see you now.

443
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:52,067
- [Pearl] I gotta get back
to the New Power Generation.

444
00:21:54,900 --> 00:21:57,067
- [Tom] Do you want me
to oscillate, ma'am?

445
00:21:57,067 --> 00:22:00,067
- [Pearl] Never ask
Bootsy Collins if you
can borrow a coat,

446
00:22:00,067 --> 00:22:01,500
- Yes?

447
00:22:01,500 --> 00:22:03,367
- we've rounded up a
number of suspects.

448
00:22:03,367 --> 00:22:05,000
- [Crow] Including Kevin Spacey.

449
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:07,500
- I'm certain some of them
are spies for the order.

450
00:22:07,500 --> 00:22:08,900
- What of the map?

451
00:22:09,900 --> 00:22:11,767
- No word. It seems...

452
00:22:11,767 --> 00:22:13,933
- [Pearl] Chilly in here,
could you turn down your guy?

453
00:22:13,933 --> 00:22:14,767
- Yes?

454
00:22:16,067 --> 00:22:17,500
- It seems they're waiting.

455
00:22:18,933 --> 00:22:19,767
- Waiting?

456
00:22:19,767 --> 00:22:21,000
- [Crow] Beat it, wavey.

457
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:23,233
- Why would the
order be waiting?

458
00:22:23,233 --> 00:22:24,800
- Well, maybe they're
waiting for the map

459
00:22:24,800 --> 00:22:27,400
to arrive from
some far-off land,

460
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:30,600
or maybe they're waiting for
some person, I'm not sure.

461
00:22:30,600 --> 00:22:34,800
- Not sure? Are you
trying, Vultare?

462
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:36,233
- Yes, your graciousness.

463
00:22:36,233 --> 00:22:38,067
- Well try harder.

464
00:22:38,067 --> 00:22:40,800
I can't have spies
hiding under every rock.

465
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:43,133
I just can't have it,
do you understand?

466
00:22:44,100 --> 00:22:45,733
- it'll be done,
your loveliness.

467
00:22:49,133 --> 00:22:50,467
- [Pearl] The hibachis
are going, sir,

468
00:22:50,467 --> 00:22:52,667
if you want to stick
around for burgers.

469
00:22:52,667 --> 00:22:54,100
(indistinct)

470
00:22:54,100 --> 00:22:56,367
- [Tom] You ordered
decaf, right ma'am?

471
00:22:56,367 --> 00:22:57,433
Pearl, carry me, okay?

472
00:22:58,867 --> 00:23:00,867
- [Crow] Are they in an
underground parking garage?

473
00:23:01,933 --> 00:23:04,167
Carry me too, Pearl.
- Come on.

474
00:23:04,167 --> 00:23:09,167
(mechanical rumbling)
(doors closing)

475
00:23:18,800 --> 00:23:19,967
- We love you, Pearl.

476
00:23:19,967 --> 00:23:21,200
You are beautiful.

477
00:23:21,200 --> 00:23:22,633
- You are beautiful
and you are wonderful

478
00:23:22,633 --> 00:23:23,700
and we love you.

479
00:23:23,700 --> 00:23:26,267
- Uh-huh, fine, whatever.

480
00:23:26,267 --> 00:23:27,767
- You gave us a mint!

481
00:23:27,767 --> 00:23:31,500
- Will you stay with us
forever and ever and ever?

482
00:23:31,500 --> 00:23:32,533
- Nope.

483
00:23:32,533 --> 00:23:33,767
Hey, Nelson.

484
00:23:33,767 --> 00:23:36,333
(all laughing)

485
00:23:37,333 --> 00:23:38,933
- Well, I'm out.

486
00:23:38,933 --> 00:23:40,300
- Yeah, I got nothing here.

487
00:23:40,300 --> 00:23:42,233
You cheatin' again, Brain Guy?

488
00:23:42,233 --> 00:23:43,200
- Course I am!

489
00:23:43,200 --> 00:23:45,767
(all laughing)

490
00:23:46,967 --> 00:23:48,433
- I gotta tell you,
guys, this is great.

491
00:23:48,433 --> 00:23:50,333
Just sitting around
with a couple of men

492
00:23:50,333 --> 00:23:52,600
doing a little male bonding.

493
00:23:52,600 --> 00:23:54,133
You are male aren't
you, Brain Guy?

494
00:23:54,133 --> 00:23:56,667
- Last time I
checked, buddy boy.

495
00:23:56,667 --> 00:23:58,800
Hey, ask your girlfriend,
she'll tell you I am.

496
00:23:58,800 --> 00:24:01,367
(all laughing)

497
00:24:02,700 --> 00:24:03,933
- No no, it's great though.

498
00:24:03,933 --> 00:24:04,867
You know, to be sitting here

499
00:24:04,867 --> 00:24:06,267
with a couple of man-sized men.

500
00:24:06,267 --> 00:24:07,533
To not have to always be

501
00:24:07,533 --> 00:24:09,833
the big clumsy
lummox all the time.

502
00:24:09,833 --> 00:24:11,267
Down here that's you, Bobo.

503
00:24:11,267 --> 00:24:13,567
(laughing)

504
00:24:13,567 --> 00:24:15,967
- Well ask your girlfriend
she'll tell you I am.

505
00:24:17,100 --> 00:24:19,700
- That doesn't
quite work, does it?

506
00:24:19,700 --> 00:24:21,067
- Hey, whip us up another bottle

507
00:24:21,067 --> 00:24:21,900
of single-malt there, will ya?

508
00:24:21,900 --> 00:24:23,933
- Can do, Mikester.

509
00:24:23,933 --> 00:24:26,600
(popping)

510
00:24:26,600 --> 00:24:27,900
- I'm sorry we terrorized you

511
00:24:27,900 --> 00:24:29,867
and tried to kill
you earlier, Mike.

512
00:24:29,867 --> 00:24:31,500
- Ah, stuff it,
you big hairball.

513
00:24:32,800 --> 00:24:34,833
I mean come on, kill
me? Who hasn't tried?

514
00:24:34,833 --> 00:24:37,467
- Yeah, that's true.

515
00:24:37,467 --> 00:24:39,400
- Wow, it's just
great to be away from

516
00:24:39,400 --> 00:24:40,633
that lawgiver for a while.

517
00:24:40,633 --> 00:24:42,300
You know he could be such a-

518
00:24:43,400 --> 00:24:44,633
- Whoa, tell me about it.

519
00:24:44,633 --> 00:24:46,567
Man, you know, someday
she's gonna tell me

520
00:24:46,567 --> 00:24:48,233
to do something, I'm
just gonna look her

521
00:24:48,233 --> 00:24:49,300
right in the eyes and I'll-

522
00:24:49,300 --> 00:24:50,700
- [Pearl] Nelson!

523
00:24:51,733 --> 00:24:54,233
(muttering)

524
00:24:54,233 --> 00:24:55,067
- Hide the hooch.

525
00:24:56,833 --> 00:24:59,300
- I'll rain horrible
fiery death on you later

526
00:24:59,300 --> 00:25:00,367
for those remarks.

527
00:25:00,367 --> 00:25:01,833
- Ha ha.

528
00:25:01,833 --> 00:25:03,500
- Right now, I have the
conclusions of my evaluation

529
00:25:03,500 --> 00:25:08,500
and I need a break from
these two chattering objects.

530
00:25:08,500 --> 00:25:10,033
Okay Brain Butt, do it.

531
00:25:10,033 --> 00:25:12,500
- No, you can't go, Pearl!

532
00:25:12,500 --> 00:25:15,767
- Please don't leave us,
please, mint giver, we love you.

533
00:25:15,767 --> 00:25:16,733
(popping)
- Whoa.

534
00:25:16,733 --> 00:25:18,133
- Weird.
- Yuck! Weird.

535
00:25:18,133 --> 00:25:19,367
- Hi guys, you miss me?

536
00:25:19,367 --> 00:25:21,533
- Eh, I'm gonna
go take a shower.

537
00:25:21,533 --> 00:25:22,367
Whoof, man.

538
00:25:23,900 --> 00:25:27,567
- Oh yeah well, ask
your girlfriend,

539
00:25:27,567 --> 00:25:29,000
she'll tell you that I...

540
00:25:35,333 --> 00:25:38,900
(instrumental theme music)

541
00:25:45,900 --> 00:25:48,400
- [Tom] Thank you. I guess.
- [Mike] Sure.

542
00:25:48,400 --> 00:25:50,967
- Master, what's this?

543
00:25:51,900 --> 00:25:53,400
- Hmm?

544
00:25:53,400 --> 00:25:56,633
- [Tom] Damn, now I have to
tell him about the bodies.

545
00:25:56,633 --> 00:25:57,833
- Perhaps it's time.

546
00:25:57,833 --> 00:26:00,133
- [Mike] For you to shut
up and let me sleep.

547
00:26:04,967 --> 00:26:07,500
- [Tom] I've invented a
device called the basement.

548
00:26:09,400 --> 00:26:10,933
- [Crow] Nice new Birkenstocks.

549
00:26:14,500 --> 00:26:15,733
- [Mike] Come on up, Mom.

550
00:26:18,400 --> 00:26:20,700
- [Tom] Hope you like
watermelon rind pickles.

551
00:26:22,667 --> 00:26:24,467
- [Crow] It's his
museum of odors.

552
00:26:26,300 --> 00:26:27,633
- [Mike] So the big
secret is he's got

553
00:26:27,633 --> 00:26:29,833
an unfinished basement
with water damage?

554
00:26:31,733 --> 00:26:32,700
- Such wealth.

555
00:26:32,700 --> 00:26:34,133
- [Tom] Is not in this box.

556
00:26:38,500 --> 00:26:39,300
- Master...

557
00:26:44,367 --> 00:26:45,200
Why do we beg?

558
00:26:47,533 --> 00:26:49,600
- It allows me to
move around freely.

559
00:26:49,600 --> 00:26:51,500
- [Crow] Like a good
pair of underwear.

560
00:26:52,633 --> 00:26:56,867
- Master, you're a spy.

561
00:26:56,867 --> 00:26:59,533
- [Mike] You're drawn
by Sergio Aragones.

562
00:26:59,533 --> 00:27:01,100
- What do you know about spies?

563
00:27:02,633 --> 00:27:03,467
- very little

564
00:27:05,100 --> 00:27:07,700
- [Tom] Okay then, what
do you know about gelatin?

565
00:27:07,700 --> 00:27:09,567
- I'm a member of the order.

566
00:27:09,567 --> 00:27:11,267
- [Crow] He bats eighth.

567
00:27:11,267 --> 00:27:12,333
- The Delta Knights.

568
00:27:13,967 --> 00:27:17,133
The order is a secret
society dedicated

569
00:27:17,133 --> 00:27:20,233
to bringing mankind
out of the dark ages

570
00:27:20,233 --> 00:27:22,000
into an age of enlightenment.

571
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:23,100
- [Mike] We want
to open the door to

572
00:27:23,100 --> 00:27:25,400
neutron bombs
infotainment and snacks.

573
00:27:25,400 --> 00:27:28,600
- I suppose you
could say I'm a spy.

574
00:27:28,600 --> 00:27:29,800
- [Tom] I'm semi-retired now,

575
00:27:29,800 --> 00:27:31,533
don't do as much
spying as I used to.

576
00:27:36,333 --> 00:27:38,333
- Delta Knights try
to achieve wisdom

577
00:27:38,333 --> 00:27:42,567
by acquiring knowledge,
judgment, compassion,

578
00:27:42,567 --> 00:27:44,400
- [Crow] Pee throwing skills.

579
00:27:44,400 --> 00:27:46,700
- I've been waiting in
this town for five years.

580
00:27:46,700 --> 00:27:48,767
- [Mike] Working at the A&W.

581
00:27:48,767 --> 00:27:53,033
- Waiting for you.
- For me? Why?

582
00:27:53,033 --> 00:27:54,200
- [Tom] I need you
to help me look for

583
00:27:54,200 --> 00:27:55,767
the guy who's really
gonna help us.

584
00:27:59,167 --> 00:28:00,900
- [Crow] I invented
staples, by the way.

585
00:28:00,900 --> 00:28:02,867
- The prophecies.

586
00:28:02,867 --> 00:28:07,033
From lands far to the north
will come a young sage.

587
00:28:07,033 --> 00:28:08,400
- [Mike] Or you.

588
00:28:08,400 --> 00:28:11,433
- Walking slow
and seeing little.

589
00:28:12,600 --> 00:28:16,133
His special sight
will open the cage.

590
00:28:16,133 --> 00:28:18,067
- [Tom] Bunch of crap, really.

591
00:28:18,067 --> 00:28:19,700
- Your coming has been foretold.

592
00:28:21,600 --> 00:28:22,900
You're from England.

593
00:28:22,900 --> 00:28:24,633
- [Crow] Which is
unfortunate, but...

594
00:28:24,633 --> 00:28:27,433
- You taught yourself to
read at the age of three.

595
00:28:28,600 --> 00:28:31,233
when I first saw you
you could hardly walk.

596
00:28:31,233 --> 00:28:32,867
Your one eye was swollen shut.

597
00:28:34,200 --> 00:28:35,467
It's quite a fair
description, I would say.

598
00:28:35,467 --> 00:28:37,600
- [Mike] You forgot
"love machine."

599
00:28:37,600 --> 00:28:39,300
- What's the cage?

600
00:28:40,800 --> 00:28:43,600
- The order has learned
that the lost storehouse

601
00:28:43,600 --> 00:28:47,100
of Archimedes is located
somewhere here in this region.

602
00:28:47,100 --> 00:28:48,900
- [Crow] You know,
somewhere around Europe.

603
00:28:48,900 --> 00:28:49,733
- Archimedes?

604
00:28:50,967 --> 00:28:53,200
- The greatest scientist
who ever lived.

605
00:28:54,300 --> 00:28:56,367
It is thought that he had access

606
00:28:56,367 --> 00:28:58,500
to the science of Atlantis.

607
00:28:58,500 --> 00:29:00,367
- The lost continent.

608
00:29:00,367 --> 00:29:01,667
- The most advanced civilization

609
00:29:01,667 --> 00:29:03,900
mankind has ever known.

610
00:29:03,900 --> 00:29:05,500
The surviving
secrets of Atlantis

611
00:29:05,500 --> 00:29:07,967
were stored in the
library of Archimedes.

612
00:29:07,967 --> 00:29:09,233
- [Tom] Mom!

613
00:29:09,233 --> 00:29:11,600
- [Baydool] In 12 BC
the Romans attacked.

614
00:29:11,600 --> 00:29:14,100
- [Mike] And pushed
down all our cheap sets.

615
00:29:14,100 --> 00:29:16,633
- [Baydool] As the
battle raged on outside,

616
00:29:16,633 --> 00:29:18,300
Archimedes struggled to preserve

617
00:29:18,300 --> 00:29:20,067
these secrets and knowledge.

618
00:29:20,067 --> 00:29:21,967
- [Tom] Let's get
that order up, people!

619
00:29:21,967 --> 00:29:25,700
- [Baydool] chose this red
book, entitled "The Right Way."

620
00:29:27,133 --> 00:29:28,800
- Show them the Corgon crystals.

621
00:29:28,800 --> 00:29:30,200
- [Baydool] It was
fabled that Archimedes

622
00:29:30,200 --> 00:29:32,700
was developing a new
weapon the Corgon crystals.

623
00:29:32,700 --> 00:29:35,767
(indistinct)

624
00:29:35,767 --> 00:29:36,600
- [Crow] Rocky!

625
00:29:37,467 --> 00:29:38,300
- Go, go, go!

626
00:29:40,633 --> 00:29:42,767
- [Baydool] As his apprentices
gathered the inventions

627
00:29:42,767 --> 00:29:45,200
and hurried them to
safety, Archimedes raced

628
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:46,433
to finish the prophecies.

629
00:29:46,433 --> 00:29:48,233
- [Mike] it's Sadie Hawkins Day!

630
00:29:51,967 --> 00:29:53,433
- Where is Archimedes?

631
00:29:53,433 --> 00:29:54,667
- Eureka!

632
00:29:54,667 --> 00:29:56,133
- Bring him, now.

633
00:29:57,367 --> 00:29:59,667
- One moment, I'm
almost finished!

634
00:29:59,667 --> 00:30:00,800
- Surrender, old goat.

635
00:30:02,067 --> 00:30:03,733
- [Mike] Oh, right
in the tomato.

636
00:30:05,067 --> 00:30:07,033
- [Baydool] In his ignorance,
an nameless centurion

637
00:30:07,033 --> 00:30:10,033
killed the greatest
scientist of all time.

638
00:30:10,033 --> 00:30:12,900
- Leave him. He's nothing.

639
00:30:12,900 --> 00:30:14,800
- - [Crow] Cock-a-doodle-doo.

640
00:30:14,800 --> 00:30:16,667
- [Baydool] It was only
by the grace of God

641
00:30:16,667 --> 00:30:19,200
that the red book survived.

642
00:30:19,200 --> 00:30:23,000
Passed down through the
ages, this book is our key.

643
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:24,067
(eerie whistling)

644
00:30:24,067 --> 00:30:25,000
- [Tom] Tea's ready!

645
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:25,933
- Just think what we could do

646
00:30:25,933 --> 00:30:27,667
if we found the lost storehouse.

647
00:30:28,733 --> 00:30:31,700
The magnificent
machines and knowledge.

648
00:30:31,700 --> 00:30:34,400
Nothing less than a
blueprint for the future,

649
00:30:34,400 --> 00:30:38,467
and you are the key
to take us there,

650
00:30:38,467 --> 00:30:39,633
- [Tom] Well, you
and this other guy.

651
00:30:39,633 --> 00:30:41,267
- When your training
is complete,

652
00:30:41,267 --> 00:30:43,433
the order will send us the map.

653
00:30:43,433 --> 00:30:44,833
- [Crow] I have hockey practice.

654
00:30:44,833 --> 00:30:47,033
- I've already taught
you many things, Tee.

655
00:30:47,033 --> 00:30:49,833
- [Tom] Has even a word
of this gotten through?

656
00:30:49,833 --> 00:30:52,333
- But there are still
many things to learn.

657
00:30:52,333 --> 00:30:54,900
- [Mike] We still haven't
cracked soap, for example.

658
00:30:56,500 --> 00:30:58,567
- [Tom] Hey, hands off
the threads, creep.

659
00:31:02,733 --> 00:31:04,733
- [Crow] Skip to
page 37 where Sonny

660
00:31:04,733 --> 00:31:06,867
and the bridesmaid
are, well, you'll see.

661
00:31:12,367 --> 00:31:14,767
- [Mike] Idiot, why did
I tell him I could read?

662
00:31:18,100 --> 00:31:19,333
Hello?

663
00:31:19,333 --> 00:31:20,167
- [Crow] And
Collinsworth grabs it,

664
00:31:20,167 --> 00:31:22,100
will you look at him go!

665
00:31:25,100 --> 00:31:27,600
- [Tom] Years later, he's
still on the first page.

666
00:31:30,200 --> 00:31:32,433
- [Mike] Kid's turned
into Nellie Oleson.

667
00:31:32,433 --> 00:31:35,933
- Now, these can put a person
to steep in no time at all.

668
00:31:35,933 --> 00:31:38,467
- [Crow] They are tiny
James Michener books.

669
00:31:43,300 --> 00:31:44,100
- [Crow] Hey!

670
00:31:49,233 --> 00:31:51,067
- [Mike] Now here's
the dead man's brains

671
00:31:51,067 --> 00:31:52,533
and here's his eyeballs.

672
00:31:54,900 --> 00:31:56,200
- [Crow] Got a new humidor.

673
00:32:01,233 --> 00:32:04,467
- [Tom] I have a wife
and family! Aaah.

674
00:32:07,233 --> 00:32:08,600
- [Mike] NRA homeschooling.

675
00:32:11,967 --> 00:32:15,533
(instrumental theme music)

676
00:32:19,000 --> 00:32:20,633
Hi, townspeople,
it's not the beggar.

677
00:32:20,633 --> 00:32:21,800
It's me, a nobleman.

678
00:32:23,167 --> 00:32:25,367
- The time has come
but the map's not here.

679
00:32:25,367 --> 00:32:27,567
Lord Vultare has intercepted it.

680
00:32:27,567 --> 00:32:30,033
Look for the moor with
a patch over his eye

681
00:32:30,033 --> 00:32:32,533
by the bakery, he will tell
us where to find the map.

682
00:32:32,533 --> 00:32:34,133
- [Tom] You mean the dumpy nun?

683
00:32:39,267 --> 00:32:41,200
- It'll be a nice
day if doesn't rain.

684
00:32:41,200 --> 00:32:43,900
- It's always a nice
day if it doesn't rain.

685
00:32:43,900 --> 00:32:45,367
- If the sun isn't too warm.

686
00:32:45,367 --> 00:32:47,367
- [Mike] So you're a
Delta Knight too, huh?

687
00:32:50,333 --> 00:32:52,600
- [Crow] He's really
rather an artless dodger.

688
00:32:55,600 --> 00:32:57,067
- [Mike] A potato-chip, why?

689
00:32:59,633 --> 00:33:02,767
(Tom quietly singing)

690
00:33:04,967 --> 00:33:05,933
- [Tee] Is it a code?

691
00:33:05,933 --> 00:33:06,867
- [Crow] I don't know, maybe.

692
00:33:06,867 --> 00:33:07,900
I'm just farting around here.

693
00:33:11,433 --> 00:33:14,433
- Recover map from
wizard Wamthool.

694
00:33:16,733 --> 00:33:18,300
who's wizard Wamthool?

695
00:33:18,300 --> 00:33:20,267
- [Mike] Ah, he's just a guy
I went to wizard school with.

696
00:33:20,267 --> 00:33:21,200
- The Mannerjay's Merlin.

697
00:33:30,233 --> 00:33:34,400
- [Tom] Yes, did a baby
Savior just get born here?

698
00:33:36,967 --> 00:33:38,933
- [Mike] Oh, someone's
not overdressed.

699
00:33:38,933 --> 00:33:39,833
- Yes?

700
00:33:39,833 --> 00:33:41,233
- We were sent for.

701
00:33:42,700 --> 00:33:43,767
- What?

702
00:33:43,767 --> 00:33:45,567
- We were sent for.

703
00:33:45,567 --> 00:33:47,100
- [Crow] Are we
in the same movie?

704
00:33:47,100 --> 00:33:48,067
- You were?

705
00:33:48,067 --> 00:33:49,200
(indistinct)

706
00:33:49,200 --> 00:33:52,533
- Yes, I'm Dr.
Ramsian De Bourgeois,

707
00:33:52,533 --> 00:33:54,533
and this is my
apprentice, Guy Alapatie.

708
00:33:55,933 --> 00:33:57,167
- [Tom] Why don't you
have a seat in the bar

709
00:33:57,167 --> 00:33:59,200
until we have a table for you?

710
00:33:59,200 --> 00:34:00,333
- The call for magi?

711
00:34:01,767 --> 00:34:02,600
- Magi?

712
00:34:03,800 --> 00:34:06,967
- Oh yes, to decipher
some important paper.

713
00:34:08,100 --> 00:34:11,367
- Oh right, of course.
Vultare's project.

714
00:34:12,700 --> 00:34:15,500
- What a wonderful
laboratory you have here.

715
00:34:15,500 --> 00:34:16,767
- Well, thank you.

716
00:34:16,767 --> 00:34:18,667
- [Mike] He's got
a personal airbag.

717
00:34:18,667 --> 00:34:20,233
- Is that the new Rasmic?

718
00:34:21,700 --> 00:34:23,600
- Yes it is, I got
it just last month.

719
00:34:25,633 --> 00:34:27,267
- [Tom] Man, am I foul today.

720
00:34:27,267 --> 00:34:29,033
- Oh please help yourself.

721
00:34:29,033 --> 00:34:31,133
- [Crow] He's an Erykah
Badu impersonator.

722
00:34:32,267 --> 00:34:33,633
- I had another
one for many years.

723
00:34:33,633 --> 00:34:37,033
It never worked but
this one I got on sale.

724
00:34:37,033 --> 00:34:38,500
And look at the lens, I mean-

725
00:34:38,500 --> 00:34:40,233
- [Mike] Hey, an ancient Servo!

726
00:34:40,233 --> 00:34:41,300
- [Tom] Cool!

727
00:34:43,633 --> 00:34:45,833
Ooh, that spittoon's
only for sharpshooters.

728
00:34:50,167 --> 00:34:52,167
- [Mike] History's
first pepper grinder.

729
00:34:54,800 --> 00:34:56,333
- Oh, Lord Vultare.

730
00:34:57,800 --> 00:34:58,767
- What's going on?

731
00:34:59,933 --> 00:35:00,800
- Excuse me?

732
00:35:01,800 --> 00:35:03,367
- Any new progress with the...

733
00:35:03,367 --> 00:35:07,400
- The map? Oh, I haven't
even begun that yet.

734
00:35:07,400 --> 00:35:10,133
Well, I was waiting for
the experts to arrive.

735
00:35:10,133 --> 00:35:12,333
- [Tom] Yes, did my,
um, test come back?

736
00:35:12,333 --> 00:35:13,967
- Who are these people?

737
00:35:13,967 --> 00:35:14,967
- The experts.

738
00:35:15,967 --> 00:35:17,767
- I am Dr. Ramsian De Bourgeois,

739
00:35:17,767 --> 00:35:19,300
and this is my apprentice.

740
00:35:19,300 --> 00:35:21,000
- [Crow] Uh, fromage.

741
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:22,267
- Don't I know you?

742
00:35:22,267 --> 00:35:24,100
- [Mike] Aren't you
me in another role?

743
00:35:25,733 --> 00:35:27,133
- What's your name?

744
00:35:27,133 --> 00:35:29,367
- Guy-
- I asked the boy.

745
00:35:29,367 --> 00:35:30,200
- Guy...

746
00:35:30,200 --> 00:35:31,200
- [Crow] Lafleur.

747
