990
00:48:33,533 --> 00:48:35,267
is easier to carry
than I thought.

991
00:48:38,367 --> 00:48:40,033
(patrons talking loudly)

992
00:48:40,033 --> 00:48:41,433
- Hi

993
00:48:41,433 --> 00:48:43,400
- [Mike] Hey, how's everything
at this table? Great.

994
00:48:45,467 --> 00:48:46,433
- [Tom] (imitates goat
bleating) Help me.

995
00:48:48,100 --> 00:48:49,267
- We need you.

996
00:48:51,233 --> 00:48:53,767
Look at you, you gorgeous beast.

997
00:48:53,767 --> 00:48:54,833
- [All] Norm!

998
00:48:56,333 --> 00:48:57,633
- [Tom] How ya doing, everybody?

999
00:48:57,633 --> 00:48:59,867
- [Crow] Sit outside
and pet our millipedes.

1000
00:49:02,900 --> 00:49:05,400
(Tom humming)

1001
00:49:07,200 --> 00:49:09,700
- [Mike] Wow, they had
Ethan Hawkes back then too?

1002
00:49:11,267 --> 00:49:14,200
- Come with me, boy. I'll show
you the time of your life.

1003
00:49:14,200 --> 00:49:15,933
- [Tom] We're going
to Camp Snoopy.

1004
00:49:19,600 --> 00:49:20,833
- Aren't you hungry?

1005
00:49:20,833 --> 00:49:22,700
- [Crow] Do you have
any Scurvy Meals?

1006
00:49:25,467 --> 00:49:26,300
- Yes?

1007
00:49:27,267 --> 00:49:28,200
- Don't I know you?

1008
00:49:28,200 --> 00:49:29,867
- [Mike] Didn't you seat me?

1009
00:49:29,867 --> 00:49:31,700
- Have I seen you before?

1010
00:49:31,700 --> 00:49:32,967
- You don't have to
be so clever here.

1011
00:49:32,967 --> 00:49:34,000
All you have to do is ask.

1012
00:49:34,000 --> 00:49:35,300
- [Tom] The first Hooters.

1013
00:49:38,267 --> 00:49:39,867
- [Crow] I'm too young for some.

1014
00:49:41,000 --> 00:49:42,467
- Is there anything you want?

1015
00:49:43,800 --> 00:49:47,367
Some dessert? Something
more to drink?

1016
00:49:48,733 --> 00:49:50,000
Something else?

1017
00:49:50,000 --> 00:49:51,900
- [Mike] 'Cause there's
a three dollar minimum.

1018
00:49:51,900 --> 00:49:55,133
- No.
- All right.

1019
00:49:55,133 --> 00:49:56,833
- [Tom] I'll take
these elsewhere.

1020
00:49:59,667 --> 00:50:02,267
- If you change your
mind, my name is Thena.

1021
00:50:02,267 --> 00:50:03,200
- [Crow] Yeah, yeah fine.

1022
00:50:03,200 --> 00:50:04,533
Look I'm probably gay so.

1023
00:50:08,100 --> 00:50:09,333
- [Mike] I call it Bluto.

1024
00:50:14,667 --> 00:50:15,700
- What are you doing?

1025
00:50:18,000 --> 00:50:20,067
- [Tom] Not getting
thrown up on, I hope.

1026
00:50:21,233 --> 00:50:22,767
- You're trying
to steal my soul!

1027
00:50:22,767 --> 00:50:24,167
- I was just drawing an image.

1028
00:50:24,167 --> 00:50:25,567
(men yelling)

1029
00:50:25,567 --> 00:50:27,000
- [Crow] Must smoke a Galois.

1030
00:50:32,667 --> 00:50:34,900
- [Mike] Ah, he's a little
woozy from not eating.

1031
00:50:39,433 --> 00:50:40,933
- [Tom] It's so awkward when
you're at the Ground Round

1032
00:50:40,933 --> 00:50:42,633
and you have to
kill another person.

1033
00:50:42,633 --> 00:50:44,367
- [Mike] Tell me about it.

1034
00:50:44,367 --> 00:50:45,167
- Thank you, friend.

1035
00:50:46,233 --> 00:50:47,033
I'm Leonardo.

1036
00:50:49,967 --> 00:50:52,767
Is this your first time
in Madam Maydeed's?

1037
00:50:52,767 --> 00:50:54,067
- Yes.

1038
00:50:54,067 --> 00:50:55,633
- And in Florence?

1039
00:50:55,633 --> 00:50:56,533
- [Mike] Wow.

1040
00:50:56,533 --> 00:50:58,433
(indistinct)

1041
00:50:58,433 --> 00:50:59,400
- A reader?

1042
00:50:59,400 --> 00:51:01,067
A man at to my own heart.

1043
00:51:01,067 --> 00:51:04,600
As a token of my gratitude,
can I buy you a drink?

1044
00:51:04,600 --> 00:51:06,133
- No, thanks.

1045
00:51:06,133 --> 00:51:07,067
- Can I get you
something to eat?

1046
00:51:07,067 --> 00:51:08,867
- [Crow] They have a Playland.

1047
00:51:08,867 --> 00:51:09,700
- Anything?

1048
00:51:11,800 --> 00:51:14,667
- [Tom] He studied at the
Royal Academy of Dan Cortese.

1049
00:51:14,667 --> 00:51:15,567
- The girl?

1050
00:51:17,100 --> 00:51:18,967
Here at Madam Maydeed's, you
can have anything you want

1051
00:51:18,967 --> 00:51:23,567
if you have the coin,
even a lovely bedwarmer.

1052
00:51:23,567 --> 00:51:25,500
- [Mike] Big guy's
sweat is good today.

1053
00:51:28,233 --> 00:51:30,000
- [Tom] He bought
his hat at Cinnabon.

1054
00:51:32,433 --> 00:51:34,633
- [Crow] He's staying
at a bed and Ren Fest.

1055
00:51:43,200 --> 00:51:44,467
- [Mike] I'm a
door-to-door Harlequin,

1056
00:51:44,467 --> 00:51:46,300
you need any
Harlequin-ing done here?

1057
00:51:54,000 --> 00:51:55,267
- Wake up.

1058
00:51:55,267 --> 00:51:56,367
- [Crow] It's time
to go to sleep.

1059
00:51:56,367 --> 00:51:58,733
(indistinct)

1060
00:52:00,633 --> 00:52:03,900
- [Tom] Eee, ooh, you,
ooh, eeh, ah, ooh. Andy.

1061
00:52:07,200 --> 00:52:09,267
- [Mike] He's trying to use
the remote control on him.

1062
00:52:13,500 --> 00:52:15,600
- [Crow] Look, there's
outdoors out there.

1063
00:52:16,500 --> 00:52:17,900
- [Tom] Vikings lost.

1064
00:52:20,600 --> 00:52:23,200
(lively music)

1065
00:52:23,200 --> 00:52:25,967
- [Mike] Oh, for
cryin' out loud.

1066
00:52:28,200 --> 00:52:30,467
Oh damn, the safety was on.

1067
00:52:33,033 --> 00:52:33,900
- [Tom] Good thing he's
not writing a Pinto,

1068
00:52:33,900 --> 00:52:35,600
it might explode.

1069
00:52:35,600 --> 00:52:37,333
(chuckling) Sorry.

1070
00:52:39,067 --> 00:52:41,600
- Thanks, for waking me.

1071
00:52:41,600 --> 00:52:43,033
- You're welcome.

1072
00:52:43,033 --> 00:52:45,133
Besides, Travis, you'd
do the same for me.

1073
00:52:46,033 --> 00:52:47,167
- Call me Tee.

1074
00:52:47,167 --> 00:52:48,100
- Tee?

1075
00:52:48,100 --> 00:52:49,200
- [Crow] it's short for R.

1076
00:52:51,467 --> 00:52:54,800
- So why did you
steal Vultare's horse?

1077
00:52:56,133 --> 00:52:58,100
- I figured he'd
have the best one.

1078
00:52:58,100 --> 00:52:59,767
- [Mike] But it
pulls to the left.

1079
00:53:01,767 --> 00:53:03,167
- Do you think we
should split up,

1080
00:53:03,167 --> 00:53:05,833
make it more difficult
for them to follow us?

1081
00:53:05,833 --> 00:53:07,167
- It depends on the weather.

1082
00:53:08,300 --> 00:53:09,533
- What do you mean?

1083
00:53:09,533 --> 00:53:12,467
- It'll be a nice day
if it doesn't rain.

1084
00:53:12,467 --> 00:53:14,800
- It's always a nice
day if it doesn't rain.

1085
00:53:14,800 --> 00:53:16,933
- If the sun isn't too warm.

1086
00:53:16,933 --> 00:53:18,133
- You're my contact?

1087
00:53:18,133 --> 00:53:19,567
- [Tom] Let me see
your tiny time pills.

1088
00:53:19,567 --> 00:53:21,200
- You're a Delta Knight?

1089
00:53:21,200 --> 00:53:22,800
- Looks that way.

1090
00:53:22,800 --> 00:53:24,800
I was born in a small
town called Vinci.

1091
00:53:24,800 --> 00:53:27,533
about 10 years ago, I
moved to Florence to study.

1092
00:53:27,533 --> 00:53:29,500
- My master is a
member of the order.

1093
00:53:32,300 --> 00:53:33,133
Oh no.

1094
00:53:35,933 --> 00:53:38,200
- You're not going anywhere
on that beast. Look.

1095
00:53:38,200 --> 00:53:39,500
Here, ride with me.

1096
00:53:43,867 --> 00:53:47,900
- [Mike] Hey, that's always
been there. I run just fine.

1097
00:53:47,900 --> 00:53:48,733
- Come on!

1098
00:53:50,500 --> 00:53:53,133
- Rather persistent,
aren't they?

1099
00:53:53,133 --> 00:53:54,700
[Crow] Leonardo barely
escaped being called

1100
00:53:54,700 --> 00:53:56,600
Leonardo da Gary, Indiana.

1101
00:54:00,400 --> 00:54:01,833
- [Tom] Yeah, then my
dad got transferred

1102
00:54:01,833 --> 00:54:04,333
and I was Leonardo da Oxnard
for a couple of years.

1103
00:54:08,033 --> 00:54:10,100
- This isn't about
horses, is it?

1104
00:54:10,100 --> 00:54:10,933
- Probably not.

1105
00:54:12,100 --> 00:54:13,333
- Are you going to tell me

1106
00:54:13,333 --> 00:54:14,567
or am I gonna have to
drag it out of you?

1107
00:54:14,567 --> 00:54:16,200
- [Mike] The horse is
wearing a modest skirt.

1108
00:54:16,200 --> 00:54:17,233
- We took something.

1109
00:54:17,233 --> 00:54:18,433
- What did you take?

1110
00:54:18,433 --> 00:54:19,600
- [Crow] A lot of
little sugar packets.

1111
00:54:19,600 --> 00:54:20,567
- The slave market.

1112
00:54:20,567 --> 00:54:21,500
- Slave market?

1113
00:54:21,500 --> 00:54:22,900
You took the slave market?

1114
00:54:23,900 --> 00:54:25,100
- I knew she looked familiar.

1115
00:54:25,100 --> 00:54:26,033
- Who?

1116
00:54:26,033 --> 00:54:30,100
- Thena. The serving girl.

1117
00:54:30,100 --> 00:54:33,233
The one Vultare just bought.

1118
00:54:34,567 --> 00:54:35,467
Turn around.

1119
00:54:35,467 --> 00:54:37,233
- What?
- Turn around

1120
00:54:37,233 --> 00:54:38,500
- [Crow] Bright eyes.

1121
00:54:38,500 --> 00:54:39,967
- I'm telling you right
now, I don't like this.

1122
00:54:39,967 --> 00:54:41,467
- [Mike] Hey, the
horse isn't wearing

1123
00:54:41,467 --> 00:54:43,200
any underpants under that skirt.

1124
00:54:46,500 --> 00:54:49,467
- [Tom] Medieval Gold,
24 madrigals by 24 stars!

1125
00:54:49,467 --> 00:54:50,467
- This way, men.

1126
00:54:51,867 --> 00:54:53,900
The last (indistinct)
must be just ahead.

1127
00:54:55,333 --> 00:54:57,400
I can't believe you idiots
let them steal my horse!

1128
00:54:58,800 --> 00:55:00,533
You'd better watch my face
more closely, Brandow.

1129
00:55:00,533 --> 00:55:02,267
- Very good, sir.

1130
00:55:02,267 --> 00:55:03,167
[Crow] they're working
as head hunters

1131
00:55:03,167 --> 00:55:04,367
for a rival tavern.

1132
00:55:07,100 --> 00:55:08,033
- [Thena] Let me go!

1133
00:55:08,033 --> 00:55:09,100
- And another thing, Brandow-

1134
00:55:10,967 --> 00:55:13,100
- [Mike] Yep, wench-jacking
was a big problem

1135
00:55:13,100 --> 00:55:14,233
during the Middle Ages.

1136
00:55:16,533 --> 00:55:17,633
- Stop, stop!

1137
00:55:21,300 --> 00:55:22,600
- It's you.

1138
00:55:22,600 --> 00:55:23,533
- Of course it is.

1139
00:55:23,533 --> 00:55:24,467
Who else would be such a fool

1140
00:55:24,467 --> 00:55:25,533
as to try and rescue you?

1141
00:55:26,700 --> 00:55:29,000
- Many real men would
give their lives for me.

1142
00:55:29,000 --> 00:55:31,467
- Why, when they could
have you for a few copper?

1143
00:55:32,900 --> 00:55:35,267
- If you think so little of
me, then why did you help me?

1144
00:55:35,267 --> 00:55:37,500
- I only helped because he-
- Stop it.

1145
00:55:37,500 --> 00:55:38,967
We don't have time for this.

1146
00:55:38,967 --> 00:55:40,767
Vultare and his men could
be here at any moment.

1147
00:55:40,767 --> 00:55:42,733
- Take the other horse,
I'll ride with you.

1148
00:55:42,733 --> 00:55:44,233
- Oh no you don't.

1149
00:55:44,233 --> 00:55:45,500
- We only have two horses.

1150
00:55:45,500 --> 00:55:47,300
- Doesn't matter, you're
not riding with me.

1151
00:55:47,300 --> 00:55:49,800
- Excuse me, little
miss princess.

1152
00:55:49,800 --> 00:55:51,600
- You're not riding with me!
- Enough!

1153
00:55:51,600 --> 00:55:53,933
I'll ride with you.

1154
00:55:53,933 --> 00:55:54,867
- [Tom] They're gonna
have to check each other

1155
00:55:54,867 --> 00:55:56,233
for ticks when they get home.

1156
00:55:58,767 --> 00:55:59,900
- Princess.

1157
00:55:59,900 --> 00:56:03,467
♪ Give us British Sterling ♪

1158
00:56:10,967 --> 00:56:15,967
- [Mike] How'd you
get a restraining
order on me so quick?

1159
00:56:17,067 --> 00:56:18,900
- [Tom] (sighing) Well,
huzzah, I suppose.

1160
00:56:21,900 --> 00:56:24,000
- [Crow] It's a Nicole
Kidman in the wild.

1161
00:56:26,467 --> 00:56:28,000
- You stole something, did you?

1162
00:56:29,200 --> 00:56:31,267
- [Mike] Hello? Hey,
mead-for-brains.

1163
00:56:32,600 --> 00:56:33,900
- what did you steal?

1164
00:56:33,900 --> 00:56:35,367
- [Tom] Pretzels.

1165
00:56:35,367 --> 00:56:39,633
- Money, jewels? A map to
the lost storehouse, perhaps?

1166
00:56:42,667 --> 00:56:43,500
- How did you know that?

1167
00:56:43,500 --> 00:56:45,400
- Oh, come on, Tee.

1168
00:56:45,400 --> 00:56:46,700
In addition to being
a pretty good artist

1169
00:56:46,700 --> 00:56:49,900
I'm great with maps
so how about it?

1170
00:56:49,900 --> 00:56:52,200
- [Mike] How great can
you really be at maps?

1171
00:56:52,200 --> 00:56:54,533
- [Crow] It's like being
good at eating cereal.

1172
00:57:00,967 --> 00:57:02,200
- Who drew this?

1173
00:57:02,200 --> 00:57:03,667
- [Mike] My grandma,
was born without arms.

1174
00:57:03,667 --> 00:57:04,533
- I copied it.

1175
00:57:05,900 --> 00:57:08,533
- Ah. A noble effort.

1176
00:57:08,533 --> 00:57:10,100
- [Tom] Yeah, for
using your butt.

1177
00:57:14,367 --> 00:57:16,100
- So. about the girl.

1178
00:57:18,367 --> 00:57:19,633
- What about her?

1179
00:57:19,633 --> 00:57:20,633
- Well, we can't very
well take her with us.

1180
00:57:20,633 --> 00:57:21,800
She'd slow us down.

1181
00:57:21,800 --> 00:57:23,833
- We can't just leave her here.

1182
00:57:23,833 --> 00:57:24,833
- We can give us some money,

1183
00:57:24,833 --> 00:57:26,267
she can take care of herself.

1184
00:57:27,300 --> 00:57:28,500
- She's coming.

1185
00:57:28,500 --> 00:57:30,333
- She's nothing but
a serving wench.

1186
00:57:30,333 --> 00:57:31,267
- That's not true.

1187
00:57:31,267 --> 00:57:32,567
- [Crow] She's a shift leader.

1188
00:57:33,700 --> 00:57:35,533
- The rules of the
order are very clear.

1189
00:57:35,533 --> 00:57:37,333
We're not just going
to abandon her.

1190
00:57:42,633 --> 00:57:43,900
- Watch this.

1191
00:57:43,900 --> 00:57:46,133
- [Mike] I'm gonna short
sheet her sleeping bag.

1192
00:57:48,400 --> 00:57:50,200
- [Tom] Can we see
the dessert tray?

1193
00:57:52,933 --> 00:57:56,533
- Come now, I think two
silvers is more than fair.

1194
00:57:56,533 --> 00:57:57,433
- I said no.

1195
00:58:02,167 --> 00:58:03,567
Doing something
when you are forced

1196
00:58:03,567 --> 00:58:05,367
and doing something
in your own free will

1197
00:58:05,367 --> 00:58:06,767
are two different things.

1198
00:58:07,900 --> 00:58:08,867
- How about three?

1199
00:58:10,667 --> 00:58:11,733
- I said no.

1200
00:58:11,733 --> 00:58:12,633
- Leave her alone!

1201
00:58:14,000 --> 00:58:15,267
- I'm no longer a slave.

1202
00:58:16,433 --> 00:58:18,567
- [Crow] Ah, I'm gonna
go design a helicopter.

1203
00:58:22,467 --> 00:58:25,033
(wolf howling)

1204
00:58:26,467 --> 00:58:28,600
- [Mike] Is that a block
and tackle for his crotch?

1205
00:58:30,033 --> 00:58:32,100
- [Crow] they pan over
and there's Balki.

1206
00:58:37,333 --> 00:58:38,767
(gasping)
(screaming)

1207
00:58:38,767 --> 00:58:40,533
- The Vikings in this
movie don't Vike very well.

1208
00:58:40,533 --> 00:58:41,600
- [Mike] Not at all.

1209
00:58:43,833 --> 00:58:46,967
(weapon firing)

1210
00:58:46,967 --> 00:58:47,800
- There's another one.

1211
00:58:47,800 --> 00:58:49,033
- Thena!

1212
00:58:49,033 --> 00:58:50,967
- [Tom] They must have
camped outside Sturgis.

1213
00:58:50,967 --> 00:58:51,900
- Vultare's scouts.

1214
00:58:53,433 --> 00:58:55,467
- I thought you
said we'd lost them.

1215
00:58:55,467 --> 00:58:58,633
- I don't know, maybe
they weren't scouts.

1216
00:58:58,633 --> 00:59:00,867
- [Mike] Well, I'm never
gonna get back to sleep now.

1217
00:59:00,867 --> 00:59:03,500
- They were scouts, all
right, but not very good ones.

1218
00:59:03,500 --> 00:59:06,233
If they'd killed us, Vultare
surely would have killed them.

1219
00:59:06,233 --> 00:59:08,167
- [Tom] And this guy
fell on our bread.

1220
00:59:12,067 --> 00:59:13,833
- Maybe they just
stumbled onto us.

1221
00:59:16,400 --> 00:59:17,533
- With the scouts dead,
Vultare will have to

1222
00:59:17,533 --> 00:59:19,067
decipher the map for himself.

1223
00:59:19,067 --> 00:59:21,267
- What?
- Nothing.

1224
00:59:21,267 --> 00:59:22,233
it's none of your concern.

1225
00:59:22,233 --> 00:59:23,167
- [Mike] Okay.

1226
00:59:23,167 --> 00:59:24,367
- We should get out of here.

1227
00:59:26,000 --> 00:59:28,367
- If it weren't for the girl,
they'd never have found us.

1228
00:59:28,367 --> 00:59:29,800
- I never asked for your help

1229
00:59:31,267 --> 00:59:33,067
- [Crow] Future
site of Euro Disney.

1230
00:59:37,167 --> 00:59:38,367
- [Tom] Well, the movie lost me.

1231
00:59:38,367 --> 00:59:40,700
It lost me and it's
trotting off without me.

1232
00:59:45,467 --> 00:59:47,600
- [Mike] "Bonanza,"
now in femme-y clothes.

1233
00:59:48,967 --> 00:59:50,467
- Sorry.

1234
00:59:50,467 --> 00:59:51,667
- [Crow] I was checking out
your cleavage from behind.

1235
00:59:51,667 --> 00:59:54,000
- For the way I treated you.

1236
00:59:56,033 --> 00:59:58,033
- [Tom] I like you.
(dopey laughing)

1237
00:59:58,033 --> 00:59:59,833
- Thank you.

1238
00:59:59,833 --> 01:00:01,367
- For what?

1239
01:00:01,367 --> 01:00:02,433
- Saving us back there.

1240
01:00:02,433 --> 01:00:04,267
- [Mike] And for your pillows.

1241
01:00:04,267 --> 01:00:06,867
- Why Leonardo, you
say the nicest things.

1242
01:00:06,867 --> 01:00:09,333
- [Crow] Yeah, that's how
they raise us in Vinci.

1243
01:00:11,067 --> 01:00:14,633
(instrumental theme music)

1244
01:00:18,933 --> 01:00:21,200
- [Tom] He needs new brake pads.

1245
01:00:21,200 --> 01:00:23,467
(shouting)

1246
01:00:26,367 --> 01:00:28,667
- [Crow] Are we being
attacked or entertained?

1247
01:00:33,300 --> 01:00:36,533
- [Tom] If only this was a
mask and not my face fungus.

1248
01:00:36,533 --> 01:00:37,633
- You're on our land.

1249
01:00:39,867 --> 01:00:42,300
- [Mike] Put on fruity
half-masks and be welcome.

1250
01:00:44,100 --> 01:00:45,067
- Come with us.

1251
01:00:45,067 --> 01:00:46,267
- [Crow] We're about to do

1252
01:00:46,267 --> 01:00:47,300
back rubs and
breathing exercises.

1253
01:00:51,600 --> 01:00:53,800
- [Tom] Mom bought me
this for trick and treat.

1254
01:00:57,400 --> 01:00:59,167
- Who are these people?

1255
01:00:59,167 --> 01:01:01,067
- I don't know, but
every moment that passes,

1256
01:01:01,067 --> 01:01:02,033
Vultare gets closer
to the storehouse.

1257
01:01:02,033 --> 01:01:03,533
- Don't let them lag behind.

1258
01:01:03,533 --> 01:01:06,533
- [Mike] And don't let
them loop their dialogue.

1259
01:01:06,533 --> 01:01:08,533
- [Crow] The tree's
infested with elves.

1260
01:01:12,033 --> 01:01:14,500
[Tom] And this winter
I'm planning on

1261
01:01:14,500 --> 01:01:17,267
being Leonardo da Cancun
for a couple of weeks.

1262
01:01:17,267 --> 01:01:18,267
- Are you all right?

1263
01:01:21,433 --> 01:01:22,433
- Who are these people?

1264
01:01:22,433 --> 01:01:23,667
- [Mike] Well, I'm Karl.

1265
01:01:23,667 --> 01:01:24,633
- I have no idea.

1266
01:01:26,733 --> 01:01:27,567
Do you?

1267
01:01:28,500 --> 01:01:29,600
- I'm not sure-

1268
01:01:29,600 --> 01:01:30,433
- Silence.

1269
01:01:32,200 --> 01:01:34,000
There'll be no talking by
Prince Jamteer's command.

1270
01:01:34,000 --> 01:01:36,467
- [Crow] Well, tell Prince
Jump-jugs we're sorry.

1271
01:01:38,100 --> 01:01:39,367
- Prince?

1272
01:01:39,367 --> 01:01:40,333
- [Mike] It's better
than being captured

1273
01:01:40,333 --> 01:01:41,633
by Morris Day, I guess.

1274
01:01:45,933 --> 01:01:47,167
- What are you doing?

1275
01:01:47,167 --> 01:01:48,333
- [Tom] Trying to
obey Prince Jump-jugs.

1276
01:01:49,500 --> 01:01:53,467
- When in doubt, rest.

1277
01:01:53,467 --> 01:01:56,100
- [Crow] You are full of
crap beyond your years, kid.

1278
01:01:58,400 --> 01:01:59,333
- [Mike] Hey, help!

1279
01:02:01,167 --> 01:02:02,633
- Open up.

1280
01:02:02,633 --> 01:02:04,200
Jamteer wants to see the girl.

1281
01:02:04,200 --> 01:02:05,667
[Tom] Well, if Jubja wants to
see the wirl, I guess we can.

1282
01:02:09,400 --> 01:02:10,333
- What's going on?

1283
01:02:10,333 --> 01:02:11,633
(indistinct)

1284
01:02:11,633 --> 01:02:13,367
- [Crow] Bent
Foliage State Prison.

1285
01:02:14,467 --> 01:02:15,300
- You leave her alone!

1286
01:02:15,300 --> 01:02:17,567
- I said back off, boy!

1287
01:02:17,567 --> 01:02:21,767
- Let me go!
- Thena!

1288
01:02:21,767 --> 01:02:23,567
- [Mike] Well, only 60
percent of their prisoners

1289
01:02:23,567 --> 01:02:24,933
break out the first night.

1290
01:02:27,367 --> 01:02:28,567
- Thena!

1291
01:02:28,567 --> 01:02:29,733
- [Tom] Can you bring
me a Klondike bar?

1292
01:02:33,667 --> 01:02:35,767
- [Crow] It's your
turn to meet Peter Pan.

1293
01:02:39,300 --> 01:02:42,100
- [Mike] This is about me not
pooling my tip money, right?

1294
01:02:44,933 --> 01:02:46,200
- Leave us.
- My liege.

1295
01:02:47,133 --> 01:02:48,000
- [Tom] My leech?

1296
01:02:50,467 --> 01:02:52,433
- Please, sit.
- Stay.

1297
01:02:55,700 --> 01:02:57,533
- [Tom] There's a midget
under her dress pushing up.

1298
01:02:57,533 --> 01:02:58,833
- [Crow] Lucky midget.

1299
01:02:58,833 --> 01:03:00,100
Midgets get everything.

1300
01:03:04,000 --> 01:03:04,867
- It's all right.

1301
01:03:06,167 --> 01:03:07,800
I'm not gonna hurt you.

1302
01:03:08,967 --> 01:03:11,133
- [Mike] Can I borrow
one of those things?

1303
01:03:13,467 --> 01:03:14,733
- Don't I know you?

1304
01:03:14,733 --> 01:03:16,600
- [Tom] Aren't you the
woman I just captured?

1305
01:03:16,600 --> 01:03:18,867
- [Prince] I think I've
seen you somewhere before.

1306
01:03:18,867 --> 01:03:22,133
- I doubt it, I've been
a slave since I was five.

1307
01:03:22,133 --> 01:03:23,500
- Since you were five...

1308
01:03:23,500 --> 01:03:26,167
- [Mike] That's a good
age to start as a slave.

1309
01:03:26,167 --> 01:03:28,800
- Tell me, what is your name?

1310
01:03:30,300 --> 01:03:31,800
- They call me Thena.

1311
01:03:31,800 --> 01:03:33,000
- [Crow] Fina, like
the gas station?

1312
01:03:33,000 --> 01:03:34,167
- Short for Athena?

1313
01:03:37,400 --> 01:03:39,367
Oh my god. My god, Athena!

1314
01:03:40,533 --> 01:03:42,367
- [Tom] Hey, I think
this is plot crap.

1315
01:03:44,200 --> 01:03:45,033
- Rando!

1316
01:03:45,033 --> 01:03:46,500
- Yes, my liege?

1317
01:03:46,500 --> 01:03:48,733
- [Prince] Sound the call, I
have great news for our people.

1318
01:03:48,733 --> 01:03:49,567
- As you wish.

1319
01:03:51,033 --> 01:03:53,300
(shouting)

1320
01:03:56,800 --> 01:03:58,633
- [Mike] Help me down!

1321
01:04:03,667 --> 01:04:05,867
- [Crow] Thanks for not
breaking the sticks.

1322
01:04:05,867 --> 01:04:06,800
- Come with us.

1323
01:04:10,733 --> 01:04:12,167
- What's going on?

1324
01:04:12,167 --> 01:04:14,033
- [Tom] Johnny Cash is
gonna entertain you tonight.

1325
01:04:15,667 --> 01:04:17,100
- Follow my lead.

1326
01:04:17,100 --> 01:04:18,967
- [Mike] Get hair extensions
and talk like a girl.

1327
01:04:22,533 --> 01:04:25,000
(villagers hooting)
- I'm going.

1328
01:04:25,000 --> 01:04:27,133
- [Crow] Gotta go visit
the howler monkeys.

1329
01:04:28,933 --> 01:04:30,500
- Now, Leonardo!

1330
01:04:30,500 --> 01:04:31,967
- [Tom] Oh, the plan is ruuuun!

1331
01:04:33,500 --> 01:04:34,833
- Where are you running to?

1332
01:04:37,267 --> 01:04:39,567
- What have you done
with these two now?

1333
01:04:39,567 --> 01:04:40,900
(high-pitched yelling)

1334
01:04:40,900 --> 01:04:42,967
- [Mike] Cheech Marin?

1335
01:04:42,967 --> 01:04:44,767
- Why did it have
to be (indistinct).

1336
01:04:44,767 --> 01:04:45,833
- They're over here!

1337
01:04:45,833 --> 01:04:46,700
- Follow me!

1338
01:04:46,700 --> 01:04:47,933
- Do I have a choice?

1339
01:04:47,933 --> 01:04:49,800
- [Tom] I'm starting
to like "Willow."

1340
01:04:51,000 --> 01:04:52,667
- I see them, I'm coming!

1341
01:04:52,667 --> 01:04:54,100
- [Crow] Oh, do you see them?

1342
01:04:55,067 --> 01:04:57,233
- Here, quietly.

1343
01:04:57,233 --> 01:04:58,733
- Quietly?

1344
01:04:58,733 --> 01:05:00,867
- [Mike] So the Ewoks grew
up to be big stupid men?

1345
01:05:02,133 --> 01:05:04,200
- I'm coming, I'm coming!

1346
01:05:06,533 --> 01:05:08,033
- Run, just run!

1347
01:05:08,033 --> 01:05:09,500
- [Crow] Unless I'm
mistaken, I'm fairly sure

1348
01:05:09,500 --> 01:05:11,567
that that one guy is coming!

1349
01:05:17,367 --> 01:05:19,067
- I'm coming!

1350
01:05:19,067 --> 01:05:21,300
(indistinct)

1351
01:05:21,300 --> 01:05:22,767
- Come on!

1352
01:05:22,767 --> 01:05:25,167
- [Mike] Snuggles the bear
is partying with his friends.

1353
01:05:29,967 --> 01:05:31,500
- There, there they are!

1354
01:05:31,500 --> 01:05:33,000
- Come on, Tee, hurry!

1355
01:05:33,000 --> 01:05:35,300
- [Crow] We're almost back to
where we first escaped from.

1356
01:05:35,300 --> 01:05:36,933
- [Tom] At least they're coming!

1357
01:05:40,133 --> 01:05:41,633
(laughing)

1358
01:05:41,633 --> 01:05:43,867
(halfhearted laughing)

1359
01:05:43,867 --> 01:05:44,967
- I'm coming!

1360
01:05:46,833 --> 01:05:49,000
- [Mike] Put a sock
in it, Legolas.

1361
01:05:49,000 --> 01:05:51,300
- I'm sorry for the way
you've been treated.

1362
01:05:51,300 --> 01:05:53,000
- You're sorry?

1363
01:05:53,000 --> 01:05:54,600
- What's going on?

1364
01:05:54,600 --> 01:05:55,833
- And I'd like to thank you

1365
01:05:55,833 --> 01:05:58,133
for bringing my sister
back to her people.

1366
01:05:58,133 --> 01:05:59,100
- Your sister?

1367
01:05:59,100 --> 01:06:00,100
- [Crow] Him or me?

1368
01:06:01,500 --> 01:06:03,933
- Perhaps I'd better let
Princess Athena explain.

1369
01:06:05,433 --> 01:06:06,500
- Princess Athena?

1370
01:06:06,500 --> 01:06:08,167
- [Crow] I'm coming!

1371
01:06:11,600 --> 01:06:13,800
- My god, Tee,
she is a princess.

1372
01:06:13,800 --> 01:06:15,300
- [Mike] Oh, her
dough has risen.

1373
01:06:18,467 --> 01:06:21,467
- Quite a change from a slattern
in a bawdy-house, isn't it?

1374
01:06:23,667 --> 01:06:24,967
Kidding.

1375
01:06:24,967 --> 01:06:26,700
- Athena was always a princess.

1376
01:06:26,700 --> 01:06:28,800
- [Crow] Or a cheerleader
or a naughty nurse.

1377
01:06:28,800 --> 01:06:32,200
- No matter what she had to do.

1378
01:06:32,200 --> 01:06:34,467
- [Tom] I just meant
she was a hooker.

1379
01:06:34,467 --> 01:06:36,500
- My two knights
in shining armor.

1380
01:06:38,200 --> 01:06:39,067
- Not so shining.

1381
01:06:40,700 --> 01:06:42,267
- [Mike] Does she have
a butt in her dress?

1382
01:06:42,267 --> 01:06:43,800
- You must be hungry.

1383
01:06:43,800 --> 01:06:45,700
I'll see that some
food is brought.

1384
01:06:45,700 --> 01:06:47,400
- [Crow] No whorin'
while I'm gone.

1385
01:06:47,400 --> 01:06:48,400
- Thank you.

1386
01:06:50,100 --> 01:06:52,600
- Prepare a feast, my
people, and rejoice.

1387
01:06:52,600 --> 01:06:54,867
Our princess has returned.

1388
01:06:54,867 --> 01:06:56,267
- You're really a princess?

1389
01:06:56,267 --> 01:06:58,700
- Yes, so Jamteer tells me.

1390
01:07:00,400 --> 01:07:03,100
This tree village serves as
my brother's hunting lodge.

1391
01:07:04,233 --> 01:07:05,533
After we eat, we have
to get some sleep

1392
01:07:05,533 --> 01:07:06,733
so we can leave at dawn.

1393
01:07:07,733 --> 01:07:09,067
- Leave at dawn?

1394
01:07:09,067 --> 01:07:11,600
- To get to the lost
storehouse before Vultare does.

1395
01:07:13,033 --> 01:07:15,533
- You know about
the lost storehouse?

1396
01:07:15,533 --> 01:07:17,700
- Yes, I heard you
talking to Tee about it.

1397
01:07:19,433 --> 01:07:20,733
- Have you told anyone?

1398
01:07:20,733 --> 01:07:22,033
- [Tom] Can we
got some crackers?

1399
01:07:22,033 --> 01:07:23,233
- No, no one.

1400
01:07:23,233 --> 01:07:26,900
- Please, Thena. I
mean, Princess Athena.

1401
01:07:26,900 --> 01:07:28,733
- You can still call me Thena.

1402
01:07:28,733 --> 01:07:30,467
- You can tell no one, Thena.

1403
01:07:30,467 --> 01:07:32,867
Please, you must promise.

1404
01:07:32,867 --> 01:07:34,300
- All right, I promise.

1405
01:07:34,300 --> 01:07:36,133
- You can't come with us.

1406
01:07:36,133 --> 01:07:37,533
- But you need help,
my brother and a few

1407
01:07:37,533 --> 01:07:38,767
of his most trusted men-

1408
01:07:38,767 --> 01:07:40,900
- No, Leonardo and
I have to go alone.

1409
01:07:40,900 --> 01:07:42,233
- [Tom] No.

1410
01:07:42,233 --> 01:07:44,000
- We belong to a secret society.

1411
01:07:44,000 --> 01:07:45,033
- The order.

1412
01:07:45,033 --> 01:07:47,333
- (scoffs) Just great.

1413
01:07:47,333 --> 01:07:48,500
- Yes.

1414
01:07:48,500 --> 01:07:50,300
As Delta Knights
we're sworn to do this

1415
01:07:50,300 --> 01:07:52,433
for the benefit of all mankind.

1416
01:07:52,433 --> 01:07:54,000
- [Mike] Except Dick Armey.

1417
01:07:54,000 --> 01:07:55,367
- I'm sorry, Thena.

1418
01:07:55,367 --> 01:07:56,700
- [Crow] I'm coming!

1419
01:07:56,700 --> 01:07:58,267
- [Tom] I'm coming!

1420
01:08:00,467 --> 01:08:05,400
(mechanical rumbling)
(doors closing)

1421
01:08:12,767 --> 01:08:14,367
- Come on, Gretzky.

1422
01:08:14,367 --> 01:08:16,733
♪ Cause I'm bad, shamon ♪

1423
01:08:16,733 --> 01:08:17,767
Ow, hey!

1424
01:08:17,767 --> 01:08:19,033
- Sorry, sorry.

1425
01:08:19,033 --> 01:08:20,867
- Hey hey, Mike, there's
some sort of a spaceship

1426
01:08:20,867 --> 01:08:22,333
approaching the port bow.

1427
01:08:22,333 --> 01:08:26,200
- Oh, Cambot, give me Rocket
Number Eleven Minus Two.

1428
01:08:26,200 --> 01:08:27,033
- Cute.

1429
01:08:35,367 --> 01:08:36,500
- Wow!

1430
01:08:36,500 --> 01:08:38,000
- Leonardo da Vinci!

1431
01:08:38,000 --> 01:08:40,000
Mr. da Vinci, it's
an honor to meet you.

1432
01:08:40,000 --> 01:08:42,633
- Hey, don't worry about
it, aight? Call me Leo.

1433
01:08:42,633 --> 01:08:43,833
And I call you?

1434
01:08:43,833 --> 01:08:46,100
- Oh, Mike and this
is Tom and Crow.

1435
01:08:46,100 --> 01:08:48,567
- Mike, Tom, Crow is it?

1436
01:08:48,567 --> 01:08:52,267
Crow? I like it,
Crow, it's good.

1437
01:08:52,267 --> 01:08:55,300
- Wow, Leo, I have to say I'm
amazed you're still alive.

1438
01:08:55,300 --> 01:08:56,567
- What, you been
talking to somebody?

1439
01:08:56,567 --> 01:08:58,000
What's so amazing
I'm still alive?

1440
01:08:58,000 --> 01:08:59,433
- I think he just
means, you know,

1441
01:08:59,433 --> 01:09:01,600
you were born such
a long time ago.

1442
01:09:01,600 --> 01:09:02,867
- What's a long time ago?

1443
01:09:02,867 --> 01:09:05,167
You know, I watch my
back, I stay alive.

1444
01:09:06,300 --> 01:09:07,933
- So you know, I have
so many questions

1445
01:09:07,933 --> 01:09:10,300
about your art, about your
incredible inventions.

1446
01:09:10,300 --> 01:09:12,433
- Or where the movie's
supposed to be taking place.

1447
01:09:12,433 --> 01:09:14,700
Everybody's English,
except maybe it's Greece.

1448
01:09:14,700 --> 01:09:16,833
you're what, Italian I assume?

1449
01:09:16,833 --> 01:09:18,900
What the heck is going on?

1450
01:09:18,900 --> 01:09:20,400
- Hey, it's a bad movie.

1451
01:09:20,400 --> 01:09:21,467
- Well, yeah but-

1452
01:09:21,467 --> 01:09:22,967
- Don't worry about it.

1453
01:09:22,967 --> 01:09:24,900
Anyway, the reason I come
by, I wanted to tell you

1454
01:09:24,900 --> 01:09:27,600
that this guy who's
playing me in the movie?

1455
01:09:27,600 --> 01:09:29,767
He's nothing like me.

1456
01:09:29,767 --> 01:09:32,600
He's a mook, he's a mama's
boy who should be home

1457
01:09:32,600 --> 01:09:34,767
with his mother and
his little sisters.

1458
01:09:34,767 --> 01:09:36,300
He's a mook, you know?

1459
01:09:36,300 --> 01:09:37,800
- Yeah, no, I agree, yeah.

1460
01:09:37,800 --> 01:09:40,133
- Hey, and I want to tell
you that I'm not a mook.

1461
01:09:40,133 --> 01:09:41,900
That's why I come by.

1462
01:09:41,900 --> 01:09:43,567
Should've called
first, I'm sorry.

1463
01:09:43,567 --> 01:09:45,067
- No, that's quite all right.

1464
01:09:45,067 --> 01:09:46,833
So you still livin' in Vinci?

1465
01:09:46,833 --> 01:09:49,967
- No, I came over in 1907.
I live in Queens now.

1466
01:09:49,967 --> 01:09:50,900
- Oh. What are you doing now?

1467
01:09:50,900 --> 01:09:53,333
You still inventing things or...

1468
01:09:53,333 --> 01:09:56,900
- Hey, I do what I
do. I'm in business.

1469
01:09:56,900 --> 01:09:57,867
Yeah, what do you do?

1470
01:09:57,867 --> 01:09:59,367
I mean Mike, who is this guy?

1471
01:09:59,367 --> 01:10:02,267
He's asking me questions,
he wants me to be dead.

1472
01:10:02,267 --> 01:10:03,533
- I didn't-

1473
01:10:03,533 --> 01:10:04,800
- What do you need
to know what I do?

1474
01:10:04,800 --> 01:10:06,133
Maybe I come over there
and show you what I do.

1475
01:10:06,133 --> 01:10:07,367
- Leo, no, Leo.

1476
01:10:07,367 --> 01:10:08,433
Come on, come on,
leave the kid alone.

1477
01:10:08,433 --> 01:10:09,633
Come on, he's all right.

1478
01:10:10,833 --> 01:10:13,167
- Okay Mike, I got
no beef with you.

1479
01:10:13,167 --> 01:10:14,567
But you talk to him.

1480
01:10:14,567 --> 01:10:15,633
